# Draft: Windows WebKit sends SameSite=Lax and Strict cookies on cross-site requests



## Environment

- Windows NT 10.0.26300.0, Node.js 24.16.0.
- Playwright 1.63.0, WebKit revision 2359: reproduced in desktop and mobile emulation.
- Playwright 1.65.1, WebKit revision 2388: reproduced in desktop and mobile emulation.
- Playwright 1.63.0 Chromium desktop and mobile emulation: expected behavior.
- This is Playwright WebKit on Windows, not a test of Safari on macOS or iOS.

## Reproduction

The accompanying `compare.cjs` runs an HTTPS server bound to loopback on port 19994. It uses `localtest.me` as the cookie's site and `127.0.0.1.sslip.io` as a different site. Both names must resolve to 127.0.0.1. All cookies are synthetic, and output contains cookie names and attributes, never cookie values. The fixture uses a self-signed certificate with `ignoreHTTPSErrors: true` only in these test contexts.

In a new directory, save the code below as `compare.cjs`, then run the following in PowerShell with Node.js, npm and OpenSSL available:

```powershell
npm install --no-save --no-package-lock playwright@1.65.1
npx playwright install chromium webkit
openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout key.pem -out cert.pem -days 1 -subj '/CN=localtest.me'
$env:COOKIE_COMPARE_PLAYWRIGHT = Join-Path (Get-Location) 'node_modules\playwright'
node compare.cjs
```

The script exits 1 when any profile fails; each JSON line reports headers, cookie metadata and whether each cookie reached the HTTPS server. Run with `playwright@1.63.0` to compare the earlier version. `COOKIE_COMPARE_ONLY=webkit` limits the matrix to WebKit. No real credentials or application session are required.

## Expected and observed

The HTTPS response sets `Secure; HttpOnly` cookies with explicit `SameSite=Lax`, `SameSite=Strict` and `SameSite=None` respectively. All three should reach a same-site request. On a cross-site credentialed fetch only the `None` control should reach the server; on an actual top-level link navigation `Lax` and `None` should reach it, but `Strict` should not. Playwright cookie metadata should report the three attributes as set.

On both tested Windows WebKit revisions, in both profiles, `context.cookies()` reports all three as `None`. The HTTPS receiver observes all three on the cross-site fetch and on the cross-site link navigation. The `None` control reaches the receiver, confirming that the cross-site request and cookie path are exercised. Chromium 1.63.0 produces the expected metadata and behavior in both profiles. The result is not limited to metadata reporting.

Self-signed HTTPS and certificate-error bypass are fixture limitations. An independent application integration test also observed the BFF's actual `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` session cookie reaching a cross-site HTTPS receiver in Windows WebKit. Root cause and behavior in real Safari remain unverified.


## compare.cjs

```javascript
'use strict';

// Изолированная диагностика: только синтетические cookies и loopback HTTPS.
// В логах только атрибуты и факт наличия cookie, без их значений.
const fs = require('node:fs');
const https = require('node:https');
const { randomUUID } = require('node:crypto');
const pw = require(process.env.COOKIE_COMPARE_PLAYWRIGHT);
const target = 'https://localtest.me:19994';
const attacker = 'https://127.0.0.1.sslip.io:19994';
const observed = new Map();
const server = https.createServer({
  key: fs.readFileSync(`${__dirname}/key.pem`),
  cert: fs.readFileSync(`${__dirname}/cert.pem`),
}, (req, res) => {
  const url = new URL(req.url, target);
  if (url.pathname === '/set') {
    res.setHeader('Set-Cookie', [
      'CompareLax=fixture; Path=/; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax',
      'CompareStrict=fixture; Path=/; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict',
      'CompareControl=fixture; Path=/; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=None',
    ]);
  } else if (url.pathname === '/observe') {
    const names = new Set((req.headers.cookie || '').split(';').map(x => x.trim().split('=')[0]));
    observed.set(url.searchParams.get('id'), {
      lax: names.has('CompareLax'), strict: names.has('CompareStrict'), control: names.has('CompareControl'),
    });
  } else if (url.pathname === '/result') {
    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
    return res.end(JSON.stringify(observed.get(url.searchParams.get('id')) ?? null));
  } else if (url.pathname === '/link') {
    const id = url.searchParams.get('id');
    if (!/^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/i.test(id || '')) { res.statusCode = 400; return res.end(); }
    return res.end(`<!doctype html><a href="${target}/observe?id=${id}">Open target</a>`);
  }
  res.end('<!doctype html><title>Cookie fixture</title>');
});

async function main() {
  await new Promise((resolve, reject) => server.listen(19994, '127.0.0.1', resolve).on('error', reject));
  let failed = false;
  for (const [name, device] of [
    ['chromium-desktop', pw.devices['Desktop Chrome']],
    ['chromium-mobile', pw.devices['Pixel 7']],
    ['webkit-desktop', pw.devices['Desktop Safari']],
    ['webkit-mobile', pw.devices['iPhone 13']],
  ]) {
    if (process.env.COOKIE_COMPARE_ONLY && !name.startsWith(process.env.COOKIE_COMPARE_ONLY)) continue;
    const browser = await (name.startsWith('chromium') ? pw.chromium : pw.webkit).launch();
    try {
      const context = await browser.newContext({ ...device, ignoreHTTPSErrors: true });
      const page = await context.newPage();
      const response = await page.goto(`${target}/set`);
      const headers = await response.headersArray();
      const attrs = headers.filter(x => x.name.toLowerCase() === 'set-cookie').map(x => ({
        name: x.value.split('=')[0],
        secure: /(?:^|;)\s*secure(?:;|$)/i.test(x.value),
        httpOnly: /(?:^|;)\s*httponly(?:;|$)/i.test(x.value),
        sameSite: /(?:^|;)\s*samesite=(lax|strict|none)(?:;|$)/i.exec(x.value)?.[1]?.toLowerCase(),
      }));
      const metadata = (await context.cookies(target)).map(x => ({ name: x.name, sameSite: x.sameSite }));
      async function result(id) {
        return page.evaluate(async ({ target, id }) => (await fetch(`${target}/result?id=${id}`)).json(), { target, id });
      }
      const sameId = randomUUID();
      await page.evaluate(async ({ target, id }) => { await fetch(`${target}/observe?id=${id}`, { credentials: 'include' }); }, { target, id: sameId });
      const same = await result(sameId);
      const crossId = randomUUID();
      await page.goto(`${attacker}/attacker`);
      await page.evaluate(async ({ target, id }) => { await fetch(`${target}/observe?id=${id}`, { mode: 'no-cors', credentials: 'include' }); }, { target, id: crossId });
      await page.goto(`${target}/return`);
      const cross = await result(crossId);
      const navId = randomUUID();
      await page.goto(`${attacker}/link?id=${navId}`);
      await page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Open target' }).click();
      const navigation = await result(navId);
      const pass = JSON.stringify(same) === JSON.stringify({ lax: true, strict: true, control: true })
        && JSON.stringify(cross) === JSON.stringify({ lax: false, strict: false, control: true })
        && navigation?.lax === true && navigation?.strict === false && navigation?.control === true
        && attrs.length === 3 && attrs.every(x => x.secure && x.httpOnly)
        && ['Lax', 'Strict', 'Control'].every((suffix, index) => {
          const expected = ['lax', 'strict', 'none'][index];
          return attrs.find(x => x.name === `Compare${suffix}`)?.sameSite === expected
            && metadata.find(x => x.name === `Compare${suffix}`)?.sameSite?.toLowerCase() === expected;
        });
      failed ||= !pass;
      console.log(JSON.stringify({ name, pass, attrs, metadata, same, cross, navigation }));
      await context.close();
    } finally { await browser.close(); }
  }
  process.exitCode = failed ? 1 : 0;
}
main().catch(err => { console.error(err.message); process.exitCode = 2; }).finally(() => server.close());

```
